>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `QUICKCHECK_TAC`

``` hol4
Refute.QUICKCHECK_TAC : tactic
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Searches for a counterexample by testing.

`QUICKCHECK_TAC` is `REFUTE_TAC_WITH [upd_search QuickcheckBackends]`:
it runs the `exhaustive`, `random` and `narrowing` backends.
`quickcheck` (see `Refute.refute`) is the corresponding function on
terms.

### Failure

Fails only if the configuration's `expect` field is not met.

### Example

>>__ load "Refute";
>> g `!xs ys : num list. REVERSE (xs ++ ys) = REVERSE xs ++ REVERSE ys`;

>> e Refute.QUICKCHECK_TAC;
>>__ drop();

### See also

[`Refute.REFUTE_TAC`](#Refute.REFUTE_TAC),
[`Refute.REFUTE_TAC_WITH`](#Refute.REFUTE_TAC_WITH),
[`Refute.refute`](#Refute.refute)
